      "message": "Can\u0027t really land this yet - it\u0027s more of an FYI. I wanted to dig into 12592, because it seems pretty serious. It turns out you can repro the failure by just calling GrConvertPixels directly, which is helpful. So I made two more versions of the unit test - one that does that, and another that uses SkConvertPixels.\n\nThe latter test passes, the former fails exactly like the Gpu test fails when PM/UPM FPs aren\u0027t found.\n\nI also did some printf debugging of entire rows of the data - we\u0027re getting lots of not-mismatched-but-still-wrong values all over the place (compared to both the pure CPU backend implementation of read/writePixels, and the pure GPU implementation with FP based PM/UPM - both of which agree on my machine).",
